            <div xml:id="d599">

                <pb facs="0641" n="523" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg523"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.512/70: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Diplomatic Agent and Consul General at
                        Tangier</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Blake</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-02-05T10:00:00+00:00">February 5, 1929—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 5—7:49 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>3. Your telegram No. 4, January 22, 6 p.m. Conditions Department’s assent mailed
                    French Resident General January 25, 1929.<anchor n="57" xml:id="d599-f1"/>
                    Latter telegraphed me January 30, 1929; taxation referred to becomes applicable
                    February 1st. All the measures definitely adopted without amendment in December
                    sessions Legislative Assembly. Promulgation by Sultan’s representative on
                    January 31st and countersignature President Committee of Control gave them
                    executive authority. Enforcement gate tax delayed by adjustment of
                    administrative dispositions until yesterday.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Blake</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
